                <head>Byrnes–Nagy Conversation</head>
                <p>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">Editor’s Note</hi>—The Secretary of State and
                    Hungarian Prime Minister Ferenc Nagy reviewed the political situation within
                    Hungary, the possible effect of the peace treaty upon it, and the attitude of
                    the United States regarding these matters. For an account of the meeting, see
                    telegram 4479 (Delsec 908), September 7, 1946, from Paris, <ref
                        target="frus:frus1946v06/pg_332">volume VI, page 332</ref>.]</p>
            </div>
        </body>
